Yes, people DO select passwords that are in dictionaries.  Even foreign
language dictionaries.  The classic way of breaking into systems was to
get the list of encrypted passwords.  You then compare this with a list
of encrypted words (from a dictionary, word list of possible passwords, etc).
When you find a match, you're in.   MANY, MANY computer break-ins were
done just this way.

